      "writtenOn": "2017-10-12T13:28:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if MAC address is passed for the device when it is pre-provisioned and this is used for dpid generation. Right now \"mac_address\" is under \"address\" in message \n \"device\" in device.proto. Since \"address\" is a \u0027oneof\u0027 proto field, if we configure any other \"address\" than \"mac_address\", we cannot derive the dpid. \nIf we move the \"mac_address\" out of \"address\" and make it mandatory to configure it device provisioning, it will facilitate a neat way to derive the dpid. Each access device will have a mac_address, so why not make it mandatory to pass it during device pre-provisioning.\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_c231d5a3",
